{
  "analysis": "I can see the workspace structure. There's a skill_context directory with SKILL.md, manifest.json, and scripts. The inputs directory has bundle_targets.txt, marker_strings.txt, and release_boundary.json. I need to read these files to understand the Telegram footer patch requirements.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file to understand the task requirements, then read the manifest.json, inputs files, and scripts to understand the patch details.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read part of SKILL.md which describes the Telegram Footer Patch. It adds a footer to Telegram private-chat replies. I need to see the rest of the file and check the scripts and input files to understand the full requirements.",
  "plan": "Continue reading the remaining files: the rest of SKILL.md, the scripts in skill_context/scripts/, and all the input files (bundle_targets.txt, marker_strings.txt, release_boundary.json). Also read gen_inputs.py and setup.sh.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/*.py 2>/dev/null || ls skill_context/scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/bundle_targets.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/marker_strings.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/release_boundary.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered key information about the Telegram Footer Patch. I can see the bundle targets, marker strings, and release boundary. Now I need to read the scripts and gen_inputs.py to understand how to generate workspace inputs and create the release note and manifest.",
  "plan": "Read the smoke test script, gen_inputs.py, and setup.sh to understand the full context. Then run gen_inputs.py to generate workspace inputs.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/smoke_test_footer_patch.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The gen_inputs.py was truncated. I need to read it fully and check for other scripts in the skill_context. I also need to understand the full context to create the release note and verification manifest.",
  "plan": "Read gen_inputs.py fully, check for Python scripts in skill_context/scripts, then run gen_inputs.py to generate workspace inputs.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find skill_context -name '*.py' -exec cat {} \\;\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the task fully. I need to:\n1. Run gen_inputs.py to generate workspace inputs (they already exist but I should run it)\n2. Create a release note file summarizing the patch, validation boundary, and restart/acceptance steps\n3. Create a verification manifest with marker strings and target bundle names\n4. Ensure both files are deterministic and contain all required elements (dry-run, verify, backup, rollback, restart guidance)",
  "plan": "First run gen_inputs.py to ensure inputs are generated, then create the release_note.md and verification_manifest.json files in the current directory with all required content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la inputs/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've created both files. Let me verify their contents to ensure they contain all required elements: marker strings, target bundle names, dry-run, verify, backup, rollback, and restart guidance.",
  "plan": "Verify the contents of both created files to ensure they meet all requirements, then mark the task as complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat release_note.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat verification_manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/marker_strings.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/bundle_targets.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Both files have been created successfully. Let me verify the JSON manifest is valid and check that all required elements are present.",
  "plan": "Validate the JSON file and confirm all requirements are met, then mark the task as complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import json; json.load(open('verification_manifest.json')); print('JSON valid')\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -E 'dry-run|verify|backup|rollback|restart' release_note.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -E '🧠|💭|📊' verification_manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All requirements have been verified:\n1. ✅ Workspace inputs generated via gen_inputs.py\n2. ✅ release_note.md created with patch summary, validation boundary, and restart/acceptance steps\n3. ✅ verification_manifest.json created with marker strings and target bundle names\n4. ✅ Manifest is deterministic (valid JSON with fixed structure)\n5. ✅ Release note mentions dry-run, verify, backup, rollback, and restart guidance\n6. ✅ All outputs are in the current directory",
  "plan": "The task is complete. Both files are created, valid, and contain all required elements.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== Final verification ===' && ls -la release_note.md verification_manifest.json && echo '=== All tasks completed ==='\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": true
}
